Filetype: Flipper EMV resources
Version: 1
# EMV BIN (leading card-number digits) : issuing bank name
#
# Looked up LONGEST prefix first, so a specific 8-digit entry beats a 4-digit one.
# For a GUARANTEED match on your own card, read it, note the "Bank: ? (BIN xxxxxxxx)"
# number, and add a line "xxxxxxxx: Your Bank" above the 4-digit section.
#
# The 4-digit UK ranges below are BEST-EFFORT — issuer ranges overlap and get
# reassigned, so a card may occasionally show the wrong name. Edit freely.

# --- Verified own cards (8-digit, override the broad ranges below) ---
44625942: Lloyds Bank
41654904: Revolut

# --- Fintech / digital ---
535522: Monzo
448309: Revolut
539962: Starling
462994: Chase UK

# --- Lloyds Banking Group ---
4659: Lloyds Bank
4008: Lloyds Bank
4506: Lloyds Bank
4658: Halifax
5411: Halifax

# --- NatWest Group ---
4751: NatWest
5301: NatWest
5334: NatWest
5487: RBS

# --- Barclays ---
4929: Barclays
4543: Barclays
5426: Barclays

# --- HSBC ---
# 4462 removed: it's a shared range (Lloyds cards like 44625942 use it too), so
# it mislabeled a Lloyds card as HSBC. A genuine HSBC 4462 card now shows
# "Bank: ?" — add its exact 8-digit BIN here if you want it named.
4571: HSBC
4048: HSBC

# --- Santander ---
5490: Santander
5300: Santander
4098: Santander

# --- Others ---
5560: Nationwide
4893: Nationwide
4913: TSB
5044: Co-operative Bank
4562: Virgin Money
